# `.env.local` is the one that matters. It is a developer's own settings - it currently pins
# VITE_PAYMENT_PROVIDER - and Vite reads it during the build, so copying it in would let
# whatever is on somebody's laptop decide what the image does, silently and in a file the
# image never mentions. The build argument is meant to be the only answer to that question.
.env.local
.env.*.local

node_modules/
dist/
.vite/
.git/
.github/
*.md
